. * HYPOTHESIS TEST FOR H1 * (Please adapt according to your needs)
.         * Estimate the effect of having a daughter on gender equality attitud
> es using OLS.
.         *
.         * The outcome variable, gender_equality, is a factor score derived fr
> om multiple SOEP attitude items
.         * using principal factor analysis. Items were reverse-coded where app
> ropriate so that higher values
.         * reflect more egalitarian gender views.
.         *
.         * The treatment variable d_daughter is a binary indicator equal to 1 
> if the respondent has 
.         * at least one daughter. Identification leverages the assumption that
> , conditional on covariates,
.         * the presence of a daughter is as-good-as-random—treated as a natura
> l experiment based on the 
.         * quasi-random assignment of child sex.
.         *
.         * Control variables include age, marital status, education level (PGI
> SCED11), household income 
.         * (in 1000€ bands), labor force status, region (NUTS1_ew), and househ
> old size (hlk0006).
.         * Standard errors are clustered at the household (hid) level.
. 
.         reg gender_equality d_daughter ///
>                 i.male age i.married i.pgisced11 ///
>                 i.income_cat i.labor_force_status ///
>                 i.hgnuts1_ew hlk0006, vce(cluster hid)

